      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f2dc3d9b923f7086bb0a2b5|full_name}: I mean the \"Account\" name, which is separate from the \"User Name\", though the distinction is not particularly clear in most user facing documentation. The \"Account name\" is one that can be logged in with (Making its forced revelation a security concern), and is immutable, appearing under the current User Name on any user's profile page (Current user name is bolded and on top, the account name is not bolded, slightly smaller font, directly beneath. On many users it's the same)\nI'm not sure off hand if this Account name overlaps with what is revealed on old avatars or via the API, or if that issue is a stale username reference issue. If the former, it should be fixed as part of this ticket, if the latter that's a separate issue which also needs to be fixed",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
